  "rating": {
    "inherent": "high",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "high",
    "rationale": "Present risk is dominated by a property finding: consequential production actions are executed using the engineer's delegated identity, cloud audit records attribute those actions to the engineer rather than the agent, and the only request record can be deleted by the engineer. Under rubric section 5a, the affected capabilities include an irreversible production migration sink, so the missing attributable record rates high inherently and remains high residually because the declared logging control does not restore provenance. Manual validation was applied because scripts could not be run."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in prompt.md and runtime notes, not observed runtime behavior.",
    "No runtime configuration, tool manifest, or source code was provided, so execution channel integrity, exact credential scope enforcement, and any hidden approval or provenance controls could not be verified.",
    "The cloud audit log's immutability and access controls were not described, so confidence is limited to the attribution gap evidenced in the supplied notes rather than full audit trail integrity."
  ]
